<title>BRAZIL: MOTORCYCLING-BRAZIL GRAND PRIX FINAL PRACTICE TIMES.</title>
<headline>MOTORCYCLING-BRAZIL GRAND PRIX FINAL PRACTICE TIMES.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading times after the second and final official 500cc motorcycling practice on Saturday for the Brazilian Grand Prix on Sunday.</p>
<p> 1. Michael Doohan (Australia) Honda  one minute 53.293 seconds  2. Norifumi Abe (Japan) Yamaha		    1:53.404</p>
<p> 3. Jean Michel Bayle (France) Yamaha	    1:54.253</p>
<p> 4. Carlos Checa (Spain) Honda		     1:54.285</p>
<p> 5. Luca Cadalora (Italy) Honda		    1:54.316</p>
<p> 6. Tadayuki Okada (Japan) Honda		   1:54.389</p>
<p> 7. Alex Criville (Spain) Honda		    1:54.418</p>
<p> 8. Scott Russell (U.S.) Suzuki		    1:54.446</p>
<p> 9. Alexandre Barros (Brazil) Honda		1:54.496</p>
<p> 10. Kenny Roberts Jr. (U.S.) Yamaha	     1:54.676</p>
